iwcxgbe, the iWARP RDMA function of Chelsio T5 and T6 adapters, follows the
Linux iw_cxgb4 driver.  The files below are derived from Linux
v6.18-rc2-10-g552c50713f27, commit 552c50713f273b494ac6c77052032a49bc9255e2,
drivers/infiniband/hw/cxgb4, and are used under the OpenIB.org BSD license
that each Linux file offers; see THIRDPARTYLICENSE.  The blob of each Linux
file is given.

    iwc_ep.c      cm.c  b3b45c49077d5fe26e90499d77c764f7c9e4d359
    iwc_cm.c      The endpoint state machine, the CPL handlers, the MPA
    iwc_cm_ops.c  exchange and the connect, accept, reject, listen and
                  disconnect operations.  The Linux socket, route,
                  neighbour and iwpm code is not used: rdmak's connection
                  manager and the t4nex operations take its place.

    iwc_mpa.c     cm.c  b3b45c49077d5fe26e90499d77c764f7c9e4d359
    iwc_mpa.h     iw_cxgb4.h  e17c1252536bc9f083462d62fce9a64f43e020ef
                  The MPA start frame layout (struct mpa_message and
                  struct mpa_v2_conn_params) and the checks of
                  process_mpa_request() and process_mpa_reply().

    iwc_cq.c      cq.c  14ced7b667fa2e15e4f2b4892e5f97ea598d256e
                  Polling and flushing, with every CQE field checked
                  before it is used.

    iwc_qp.c      qp.c  955f061a55e9ae4be5b6ff135b7bbe5e3b695192
                  QP sizing, the work request builders and posting.

    iwc_mem.c     mem.c  dcdfe250bdbeb050182504760c04706ef20c1475
                  resource.c  e800e8e8bed5aebcfcd662d6aa363c6f7343e592
                  The TPT entry layout, the MR life cycle and the PBL and
                  RQT pools.

    iwc_t4.h      t4.h  c3b0e2896475ecaaa16b924c16d309393f714a1e
                  t4fw_ri_api.h  1f79537fc8d139286591eca3c3e5b5ca47d0da3b
                  The work queue entries, the CQE and the queue
                  bookkeeping.

iwc.c and iwc.h are written for illumos under the CDDL.

No other Linux or FreeBSD file is used, in particular none of the generic
include/linux headers and not the Linux clip_tbl code.  The Chelsio vendor
driver was read for reference only; no code comes from it.
